  mel_title: "Your Melody",
  mel_intro: "Every wallet address carries its own melody — an 8-note phrase derived from the address itself, following a public recipe anyone can recompute (see the FAQ). It is an identity, not an asset: it grants no claim, bonus or value.",
  mel_notes_label: "Notes",
  mel_number: "Melody No. {n}",
  mel_no_number: "Your Melody number is assigned when you register for Prelude.",
  mel_play: "Play my melody",
  mel_stop: "Stop",
  mel_playing: "Playing your melody…",
  mel_latest_btn: "Play the latest melodies",
  mel_latest_playing: "Playing melody {cur} of {total}…",
  q16: "What is Your Melody?",
  a16: "Your Melody is a unique 8-note phrase that belongs to your wallet address. It is derived publicly from the address itself: take the keccak-256 hash of the address's 20 bytes; the first eight bytes, in order, choose the notes from the C major pentatonic scale (C D E G A across two octaves), and the next eight bytes set each note's length (half a beat or a full beat). Anyone can recompute the melody of any address with this same recipe — nothing is stored, assigned in secret or kept on a server, in line with Open Score. Your Melody never plays on its own: it only sounds when you press Play, and you can stop it at any moment. It is an identity and experience feature only: it carries no claim, no bonus, no allocation and no monetary value.",
  q17: "Is there a referral program?",
  a17: "There are two separate referrals. (1) Prelude referral (phase 1): after you register, you get a personal link. For every person who registers for Prelude through your link, 100 OPUS is credited to you from a 5,000,000 OPUS referral pool carved out of the Prelude bonus allocation (the flat Prelude bonus pool is the remaining 15,000,000 OPUS). At most 50 registrations per referrer are counted, so the most one referrer can be credited is 5,000 OPUS. The referrer is recorded on-chain when the person registers — the on-chain record alone is what counts; the person you brought does not need to buy anything for the credit to exist. The credit is paid only if the sale graduates, through the same Merkle distributor and 30-day claim window as the other community rewards, and unclaimed shares are burned. Registering through a link costs the new registrant nothing. (2) Sale referral (phase 2): during the sale, 5,000 OPUS for every Pass sold through your referral, paid from the separate 25,000,000 OPUS referral allocation; the referrer must hold at least one Pass. Referral accrual stops at a pool cap of 15,000,000 OPUS; the rest of the allocation funds the AgentQuest badge perk (see the next question).",
  q19: "Is there a perk for AgentQuest badge holders?",
  a19: "Yes — an official partnership perk, written into the sale contract itself. If the wallet that claims a Pass holds at least one AgentQuest badge at the moment of the claim, it receives a bonus of 5,000 OPUS for that Pass, paid in the same transaction as the claim — on the Premiere path and on the Encore path alike. At most 10 Passes per wallet earn the bonus. Bonuses are paid from a fenced pool of 10,000,000 OPUS inside the 25,000,000 OPUS referral allocation, in claim order while the pool lasts. The sale contract checks the badge balance directly on the AgentQuest badge contract (0x26AD277193ff31BD086a47BF7B1d25a93573c989) — there is no list and no manual review. Like every claim, the bonus is paid only if the sale graduates. The pool divides exactly into 2,000 whole bonuses, so a remainder below 5,000 OPUS can never occur; once the pool is empty, claims simply proceed without a bonus, and the bonus logic can never block a claim.",
 q20: "What is VERS?",
 a20: "VERS is a companion token minted by the sale contract to the buyer's wallet at the moment of a primary purchase — 10 VERS for every 1 USDT paid (a Tier 1 Pass mints 10, Tier 2 mints 15, Tier 3 mints 20; at most 70,000 VERS can ever exist, reached only at a full sell-out). VERS has no liquidity pool, no official price and no buyback; SYMPHONY will never create a pool for it. Its single promised use is conditional: if Scherzo (Season 2, planned) opens, VERS converts 1:1 into VERT — the activity score an account accumulates inside Scherzo — as a bonus on top of Scherzo's own earning rules. VERS is a normal transferable token, but it is not attached to your Pass: if you sell a Pass on the official market, your VERS stays in your wallet — it moves only if you send it yourself. If the sale fails, refunds return your USDT in full and the VERS simply remains with you as a souvenir with no function.",
  q18: "What are the seasons — Rhapsody and Scherzo?",
  a18: "SYMPHONY is composed as a series of movements, and each movement is one season. Rhapsody No. 1 — the first movement · Season 1 — is the current edition: the Prelude registration, Soundcheck and the Pass sale described on this site. Scherzo — the second movement · Season 2 — is planned as the next edition, but planned is not promised: no dates, numbers or mechanics for Scherzo exist, and none are announced. The one fact about Scherzo that is already fixed is written in the Season 1 contracts: every wallet that claims through the Encore path receives a soulbound SCHERZO key NFT — exactly one per wallet, minted on its first Encore claim — which is the key to a guaranteed Overture (Tier 1) seat in Scherzo if it opens; the key registry is recorded on-chain.",
